<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Emirate of Kish</h1><p class="st-meta">1100 CE – 1229 CE (approx.) · capital Kish</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A seafaring island emirate in the Persian Gulf that dominated trade between Iraq, India and Arabia in the 12th century.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>As the port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siraf">Siraf</a> declined after its 10th-century earthquake, merchants and sea captains on the island of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kish">Kish</a>, called <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qays">Qays</a> in Arabic, took over its trade. By around 1100 a local dynasty, the Banu Qaysar, ruled an independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> there.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kish">Kish</a> lived from maritime commerce and from levying ships passing through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-gulf">Gulf</a>, and it maintained a fleet that raided rival ports and even attacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden">Aden</a> in 1135. It controlled the pearl fisheries and at times the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sheikhdom-of-bahrain">Bahrain</a> islands. Geographers such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yaqut-al-hamawi">Yaqut</a> describe its markets and its rulers' wealth, but its internal history is poorly recorded.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1229 the island was conquered by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salghurids">Salghurid</a> atabegs of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fars">Fars</a> with help from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-ormus">Kingdom of Ormus</a>, which then inherited much of its trade.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="emirate, 1100 CE – 1229 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">emirate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Arabia and the Gulf</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:81.59%;width:2.57%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1100 CE – 1229 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kish</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Persian, Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/iran">Iran</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Qays, Qays, Kish</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1164&amp;focus=emirate-of-kish" aria-label="Emirate of Kish on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5825 995 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Emirate of Kish lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6145 1251L6485 1440"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6485 1440h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6145 1251h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6145 1251h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Kish. <a href="/atlas?year=1164&amp;focus=emirate-of-kish">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

